  "database": "rschema_0026",
  "nl_text": "The rschema_0026 database is designed to manage the production, inventory, and sales of textiles, as well as the performance evaluation of employees within a company. The Textile table stores information about each type of textile, including its name, price, production date, unique ID, and type. The Department table contains details about each department within the company, such as its name, manager, and contact information, identified by a unique department ID. The Inventory table tracks the quantity of each textile in stock, including the time it was stocked, and links each item to its corresponding textile ID in the Textile table. The Employee table stores information about each employee, including their department ID, name, phone number, position, and gender, and is linked to the Department table through the department ID. The Production_Relationship table records the production history of each textile, including the producer's ID, production time, and quantity produced, and links each entry to the Textile and Employee tables. The Sales_Relationship table tracks the sales of each textile, including the customer, sales personnel ID, sales time, and quantity sold, and links each entry to the Textile and Employee tables. The Performance_Evaluation table stores the performance evaluation of each employee, including their ID, evaluation date, score, and a unique performance ID, and is linked to the Employee table through the employee ID.",
  "gold_question": "A textile enterprise needs to manage the production, inventory, and sales of textiles. Each textile has information such as name, type, production date, and price. The enterprise has multiple departments, and each department has a name, manager, and contact information. Employee management includes employee ID, name, gender, phone, and position. For each production, the system needs to record the produced product, quantity, producer, and production time. For inventory management, the system should record the products in stock, quantity, and stock-in time. For sales, the system should record the products sold, quantity, sales personnel, customer, and sales time. The system should also support performance evaluation for each department. The performance evaluation should record the evaluation date and performance score of each employee.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0026.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0026\nCREATE TABLE `textile` (\n  `textile_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `production_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`textile_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `department` (\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `manager` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`department_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `inventory` (\n  `inventory_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `textile_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `stocked_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`inventory_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `inventory_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`textile_id`) REFERENCES `textile` (`textile_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `department` (`department_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `production_relationship` (\n  `production_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `textile_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `production_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `quantity_produced` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`production_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `production_relationship_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`textile_id`) REFERENCES `textile` (`textile_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `production_relationship_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sales_relationship` (\n  `sales_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `textile_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `sales_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `quantity_sold` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sales_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_relationship_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`textile_id`) REFERENCES `textile` (`textile_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_relationship_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `performance_evaluation` (\n  `performance_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `evaluation_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`performance_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `performance_evaluation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
